  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">To strengthen the health system in Nigeria through targeted interventions that support the federal government to effectively coordinate health investment at all levels for HIV, TB and malaria (ATM) services by 2030 - Nigeria (01-Jan-2024-31-Dec-2026)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nigeria, RSSH, Lagos State Ministry of Health (LSMOH)This program has the following goals: To strengthen the health system in Nigeria through targeted interventions that support federal government to effectively coordinate health investment at all levels for HIV,TB and Malaria (ATM)  services by 2030. The objectives of this program are: Improve coordination of health financing functions at Federal and State level and  ensure financial protection for most vulnerable population by contributing to the health insurance scheme..  Advance ATM integrated service delivery in the broader RMNCH platform.  Quality improvement and service expansion at health facility and community level.  Improve the health information management system (including e-reporting).  Improve the logistics information management system.  Improve lab system - including on addreditationa nd quality assurance</narrative>
  </description>
